equals() MethodThe equals() method is defined in the Object class and is used to compare the logical equality of two objects. Many Java classes such as String, Integer, and ArrayList override this method to compare object contents instead of memory references.Widely used for comparing String and wrapper objects. Provides logical equality instead of reference equality.
